# Peppol XML Validation

When creating or modifying Peppol catalogue XML files, **always validate** them using the project's validation script.

## Validation Command

```bash
python peppol-transformer/scripts/validate_peppol_catalogue.py <path-to-xml>
```

## When to Validate

- After creating a new Peppol catalogue XML
- After modifying an existing Peppol catalogue XML
- After running XSLT transformations that produce Peppol XML output

## Common Validation Issues

- Invalid `listID` values (use UNCL7143 codes)
- Missing required elements
- Invalid date formats
- Incorrect namespace declarations

## Example

```bash
python peppol-transformer/scripts/validate_peppol_catalogue.py output/BIM2BOM_Peppol_Catalogue.xml
```

The validator uses the official Peppol validator API at `validator.logiq.no`.
